/* book: the chapter, paragraph by paragraph (first sentences):
   - A line replaceable unit (LRU) is a sealed box that can be removed and replaced on the flight line with hand tools and a short functional test, without a hangar visit.
   - In a federated architecture each function owns its own LRU.
   - Integrated modular avionics (IMA) replaces many single-function boxes with a few cabinets or racks.
   - Each hosted function runs in a partition.
   - U is the processor utilisation in per cent; tᵢ is the time window of partition i in ms; TMF is the major frame in ms.
   - Redundancy does not go away with IMA.
   - Built-in test equipment (BITE) is the circuitry and software inside each LRU or module that checks it.
   - Answer.
*/
